{"abstract":"Science and Technology Studies (STS) is a flourishing interdisciplinary field that examines the transformative power of science and technology to arrange and rearrange contemporary societies. The Handbook of Science and Technology Studies provides a comprehensive and authoritative overview of the field, reviewing current research and major theoretical and methodological approaches in a way that is accessible to both new and established scholars from a range of disciplines. This new edition, sponsored by the Society for Social Studies of Science, is the fourth in a series of volumes that have defined the field of STS. It features 36 chapters, each written for the fourth edition, that capture the state of the art in a rich and rapidly growing field. One especially notable development is the increasing integration of feminist, gender, and postcolonial studies into the body of STS knowledge. The book covers methods and participatory practices in STS research; mechanisms by which knowledge, people, and societies are coproduced; the design, construction, and use of material devices and infrastructures; the organization and governance of science; and STS and societal challenges including aging, agriculture, security, disasters, environmental justice, and climate change.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Vertesi, Janet","Ribes, David","Forlano, Laura","Loukissas, Yanni","Cohn, Marisa"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384750"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Georgia Institute of Technology","Illinois Institute of Technology","Princeton University","University of Washington"],"keyword":["Design","Digital technologies","ICTs","STS"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"engaging designing and making digital technologies","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-384750","ids":["itu-ec7a457b-17c5-4df2-89de-26de15776f76"],"keyword":["Design","Digital Technologies","ICTs","STS"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1D5F36801F0CD2FAB58396F39627E7F6"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"princeton university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Princeton University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of washington","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Washington","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"illinois institute of technology","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Illinois Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"georgia institute of technology","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Georgia Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Janet","key":"vertesipau","last":"Vertesi","name":"Vertesi, Janet","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"David","key":"ribespau","last":"Ribes","name":"Ribes, David","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Laura","key":"forlanopau","last":"Forlano","name":"Forlano, Laura","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Yanni","key":"loukissaspau","last":"Loukissas","name":"Loukissas, Yanni","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Marisa","key":"cohnpau","last":"Cohn","locid":"e9d14210-bc71-4824-b7cf-fd1448d022ab","name":"Cohn, Marisa","orcid":"0000-0002-3912-2166","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"edition":"Fourth","isbn":["9780262035682","0262035685"],"pages":"169-194","publisher":"MIT Press","status":"p","title":"The Handbook of Science and Technology Studies"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ec7a457b-17c5-4df2-89de-26de15776f76"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Engaging, Designing and Making Digital Technologies","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384750","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Design and maintenance, as categories, are related through their presumed contrasting temporalities. What do we learn about these purifications as they play out over the course of a technological object’s lifetime? Drawing on fieldwork examining the operations of a longstanding spacecraft, Cohn exposes definitions of repair and design through their temporal and affective alignment.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Cohn, Marisa"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383910"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Anthropology","Design practice","Lifetimes","Maintenance","Repair","STS"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"lifetime issues temporal relations of design and maintenance","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83025779/272_cohn_lifetime_issues_temporal_relations_of_design_and_maintenance.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383910","ids":["itu-b56cdbcd-6d5b-4f2c-82cc-dff92ceb6888"],"keyword":["STS","anthropology","design practice","lifetimes","maintenance","repair"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-35F23C9EFB9A4EBF23C44E07A5311C7F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"GNU GPL","type":"rem","url":"http://continentcontinent.cc/index.php/continent/article/view/272","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83025779/272_cohn_lifetime_issues_temporal_relations_of_design_and_maintenance.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marisa","key":"cohnpau","last":"Cohn","locid":"e9d14210-bc71-4824-b7cf-fd1448d022ab","name":"Cohn, Marisa","orcid":"0000-0002-3912-2166","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["21599920"],"issue":"6.1","journal":"continent.","pages":"4-12","publisher":"Continent","status":"p","title":"continent.","volume":"R3PAIR"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b56cdbcd-6d5b-4f2c-82cc-dff92ceb6888"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"\"Lifetime Issues\": Temporal Relations of Design and Maintenance","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383910","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"This paper discusses the empirical case of an aging and obsolescent infrastructure supporting a space science mission that is currently approaching a known end. Such a case contributes to our understanding of the degrading path at the end-of-life of an infrastructure. During this later stage in the life of infrastructure we can observe common issues associated with aging infrastructures – hardware’s material decay, programming languages and software tools reaching end of support, obsolete managerial methodologies, etc. Such a case of infrastructural decay reveals how work of infrastructure maintenance may reach the limits of repair and shift from repair-as-sustaining into a mode of repair- into-decay, actively working towards the end-of-life. What this reveals is that, rather than infrastructural decay being a natural by-product of time’s passing, there is active work that goes into producing a convivial decay in which the multiple temporalities of aging and decay are brought into alignment through negotiation of what aging means, its impacts on different forms of work, and even what counts as old and new.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Cohn, Marisa"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381575"],"event":{"acronym":"CSCW","title":"ACM Conference on Computer Supported Cooperative Work"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Infrastructure studies","Life cycles","Lifetimes","Longevity","Maintenance","Materiality","Repair","Sustainability","Temporalities"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"convivial decay entangled lifetimes in a geriatric infrastructure","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83324816/1511_cohn.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381575","identifier":[{"id":"84963632429","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-1429b627-1b9d-458c-bf1a-0e3cfba18285"],"keyword":["infrastructure studies","life cycles","lifetimes","longevity","maintenance","materiality","repair","sustainability","temporalities"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-82846382C1093F540F8300803A343C33"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83324816/1511_cohn.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","The Department, Interdisciplinary Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marisa","key":"cohnpau","last":"Cohn","locid":"e9d14210-bc71-4824-b7cf-fd1448d022ab","name":"Cohn, Marisa","orcid":"0000-0002-3912-2166","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2818048.2820077","isbn":["9781450335928"],"pages":"1511-1523","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"CSCW '16","title":"Proceedings of ACM Conference on Computer Supported Collaborative Work &amp; Social Computing"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84963632429"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-1429b627-1b9d-458c-bf1a-0e3cfba18285"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Convivial Decay : Entangled Lifetimes in a Geriatric Infrastructure","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381575","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Hardware decays, software obsolesces, infrastructures sediment, devices patinate. While recent scholarship has examined longevity and sustainability, we have little empirical understanding of how things age, decay, and obsolesce and how we might approach impermanence as a resource for practice and reflection. This one-day NordiCHI'16 workshop will bring together researchers from the fields of design, HCI, and anthropology, in order to unpack the temporalities of these forms of impermanence from both theoretical and practical perspectives. The workshop aims to build a rich lexicon for the material and temporal qualities of aging, decay, degradation, and obsolescence by drawing together participants from a broad range of domains working to develop, maintain, or study systems as they age. Drawing together these different perspectives we will consider the various ways that impermanence might serve as a resource for design, use, and maintenance of long-lived technological artifacts.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","Cohn, Marisa","Boer, Laurens","Fernaeus, Ylva","Vallgårda, Anna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384283"],"event":{"acronym":"NordiCHI","title":"Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","KTH Royal Institute of Technology"],"keyword":["Aging Technologies","Impermanence in Design","Material Degradation","Obsolescence Studies","Temporalities"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"things fall apart unpacking the temporalities of impermanence for hci","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84997470871","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384283","identifier":[{"id":"84997470871","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-cdee80f4-e354-4cea-8208-ca75d08824bd"],"keyword":["Aging Technologies","Impermanence in Design","Material Degradation","Obsolescence Studies","Temporalities"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A0BCC285ECE893BAA85ACAF1ADF66162"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"kth royal institute of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KTH Royal Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","The Department, TiP and Games Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"tsaknakipau","last":"Tsaknaki","name":"Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marisa","key":"cohnpau","last":"Cohn","locid":"e9d14210-bc71-4824-b7cf-fd1448d022ab","name":"Cohn, Marisa","orcid":"0000-0002-3912-2166","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ylva","key":"fernaeuspau","last":"Fernaeus","name":"Fernaeus, Ylva","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"vallgårdapau","last":"Vallgårda","locid":"2fa5dc89-7d78-45d0-96c7-e8f39b78dd3e","name":"Vallgårda, Anna","orcid":"0000-0001-9898-8106","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2971485.2987680","eisbn":["9781450347631"],"place":"New York, USA","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 9th Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction (NordiCHI '16)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84997470871"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-cdee80f4-e354-4cea-8208-ca75d08824bd"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Things Fall Apart: Unpacking the Temporalities of Impermanence for HCI","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384283","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Since the publication of Phil Agre’s [1] seminal work on critical technical practice, the sites of intersection between computation and society have multiplied, and so too have the sociotechnical borderlands we inhabit. Critical methodologies such as “critical design” [8,6,5], “reflective design” [3,4,7,9,15,12], “critical making” [11,6,7], “located accountability” [13, 14], “feminist HCI” [2], and “postcolonial computing” [10] have proliferated and are being taken up in increasingly diverse political, cultural and social contexts. As the sites of critical praxis have multiplied, new regimes like big data and social computing pose new challenges. Given the fluidity of the landscape it is important for us to articulate the specificities of our scholarly borderlands. By bringing together junior and senior scholars we aim to provide a forum for researchers in this area to learn from each other how to navigate changing terrains of technology research and design. To maximize in- depth collaboration between junior and senior scholars, we propose a format that includes in-depth mentoring sessions, panel presentations from junior and senior participants, group activities, and working sessions for steps forward. The goal of the proposed workshop is to foster cohesion and build mentoring relationships within the community by creating a space for open and honest dialogue about the challenges of conducting critical research and design practice. Outcomes from this workshop will be a shared knowledge base about praxis, tracing the trajectories, continuities, traversals and inheritances of critical sociotechnical research over the past decade, as well as strengthening of the critical technical practice community by way of establishing lasting mentorship relations.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Lindtner, Silvia","Cohn, Marisa","Leahu, Lucian","Holmer, Hrönn","Di Salvo, Carl"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384288"],"event":{"end":"2015-08-21","place":"Aarhus, dk","start":"2015-08-17","title":"Critical Alternatives 2015","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Cornell University","Georgia Institute of Technology","University of Michigan"],"keyword":["Critical methodologies","Critical research and design","Critical technical practice","Mentoring relationships","Sociotechnical borderlands"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"shifting borderland of technoscience tracing trajectories of critical practice","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-384288","ids":["itu-ce108bff-0074-4878-95de-8500a44b0edf"],"keyword":["Critical methodologies","Critical research and design","Critical technical practice","Mentoring relationships","Sociotechnical borderlands"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-E84348BBB9688B22ED70B8EE7CFC9732"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"university of michigan","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Michigan","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","The Department, Interdisciplinary Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"cornell university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Cornell University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"georgia institute of technology","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Georgia Institute of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Silvia","key":"lindtnerpau","last":"Lindtner","name":"Lindtner, Silvia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marisa","key":"cohnpau","last":"Cohn","locid":"e9d14210-bc71-4824-b7cf-fd1448d022ab","name":"Cohn, Marisa","orcid":"0000-0002-3912-2166","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lucian","key":"leahupau","last":"Leahu","name":"Leahu, Lucian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Hrönn","key":"holmerpau","last":"Holmer","name":"Holmer, Hrönn","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Carl","key":"disalvopau","last":"Di Salvo","name":"Di Salvo, Carl","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.7146/aahcc.v1i1.21471","isbn":["24457221"],"pages":"1-4","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of The Fifth Decennial Aarhus Conference 17- 21 August 2015, Aarhus, Denmark","title":"Critical Alternatives","volume":"II"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ce108bff-0074-4878-95de-8500a44b0edf"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Shifting Borderland of Technoscience : Tracing Trajectories of Critical Practice","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384288","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"In taking into account the ways in which material and social realms are constitutively entangled within organizations, it is rhetorically tempting to say that technologies and social structures reconfigure each other. But what does it mean to reconfigure? How does one \"figure\" the other and how do we fully embrace a mutually constitutive relationship when examining fluid relations? This paper delves into these questions by exploring how physical, social, material, technological, and organizational arrangements dynamically reconfigure each other in the duration of organizational practice. Using the venue of space exploration, we present three empirical examples from an ethnographic engagement with a NASA mission orbiting an outer planet in the solar system to examine various configurations and sociomaterial relations. In this endeavor, we suggest that theoretical and empirical traction can be gained by focusing attention on the dynamic reconfigurations between social and material realms. In so doing, we call attention to the ways in which current sociomaterial perspectives have difficulty articulating the shifting, figural, asymmetric and dynamic negotiations between people, social structures, information technologies, and representational objects. This paper contributes to current discussions of sociomaterial relations in information systems research by presenting an empirical treatment of entangled and shifting reconfigurations and providing language for engaging with this perspective.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Cohn, Marisa"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383862"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of California"],"keyword":["Dynamic reconfiguration","Organizational processes","Sociomateriality","Software Studies","outer planetary exploration","qualitative empirical analysis","representational practices"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dynamic reconfiguration in planetary exploration a sociomaterial ethnography","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84908397067","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383862","identifier":[{"id":"84908397067","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-b1e121a5-0567-4991-b517-8a4736cbbe02"],"keyword":["dynamic reconfiguration","organizational processes","outer planetary exploration","qualitative empirical analysis","representational practices","sociomateriality","software studies"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-ECAE555D5DD124732D2C77C246B01FF2"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of california","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marisa","key":"cohnpau","last":"Cohn","locid":"e9d14210-bc71-4824-b7cf-fd1448d022ab","name":"Cohn, Marisa","orcid":"0000-0002-3912-2166","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["02767783"],"issue":"3","journal":"MIS Quarterly","pages":"831-848","publisher":"MIS Research Center","publisher_org":"M I S Research Center","status":"p","title":"MIS Quarterly","title_org":"M I S Quarterly","volume":"38"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b1e121a5-0567-4991-b517-8a4736cbbe02"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Dynamic Reconfiguration in Planetary Exploration : A Sociomaterial Ethnography","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383862","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Editor's Note: In this contribution to the series on Hackers, Makers, and Engineers, she tells us about her research on relationships to technological change in a long-lived NASA-ESA software infrastructure project. Her research considers how people live alongside technological change, inhabit the temporal rhythms of computing work, and approach concerns of legacy, inheritance, and survival of computational practices as they contemplate the end of life of the mission.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Cohn, Marisa"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384685"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Engineering Studies","Infrastructure studies","Obsolescence","Organizational ethnography","STS","long lived systems"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"engineering obsolescence","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"rem","url":"http://ethnographymatters.net/blog/2014/04/21/engineering_obsolescence/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384685","ids":["itu-e7ea6cd7-10cc-4436-a2df-11b08507c8f1"],"keyword":["STS","engineering studies","infrastructure studies","long-lived systems","obsolescence","organizational ethnography"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-80E352C150FA001BA53142A3A17FFA89"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"rem","url":"http://ethnographymatters.net/blog/2014/04/21/engineering_obsolescence/","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marisa","key":"cohnpau","last":"Cohn","locid":"e9d14210-bc71-4824-b7cf-fd1448d022ab","name":"Cohn, Marisa","orcid":"0000-0002-3912-2166","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"X"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Undefined"]},"sid":["itu-e7ea6cd7-10cc-4436-a2df-11b08507c8f1"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Engineering Obsolescence","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384685","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"In a study of users' interactions with Siri, the iPhone personal assistant application, we noticed the emergence of overlaps and blurrings between explanatory categories such as \"human\" and \"machine\". We found that users work to purify these categories, thus resolving the tensions related to the overlaps. This \"purification work\" demonstrates how such categories are always in flux and are redrawn even as they are kept separate. Drawing on STS analytic techniques, we demonstrate the mechanisms of such \"purification work.\" We also describe how such category work remained invisible to us during initial data analysis, due to our own forms of latent purification, and outline the particular analytic techniques that helped lead to this discovery. We thus provide an illustrative case of how categories come to matter in HCI research and design.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Leahu, Lucian","Cohn, Marisa","March, Wendy"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382075"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Intel Labs","University of California"],"keyword":["Category Work","Data Analysis Techniques","Explanatory Categories","Human Computer Interaction HCI","Human Machine Interaction","Purification Work","Science and Technology Studies STS","Siri"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how categories come to matter","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84877945115","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382075","identifier":[{"id":"84877945115","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-36c4b47b-7301-4a90-9d8f-df47395749fa"],"keyword":["Category Work","Data Analysis Techniques","Explanatory Categories","Human-Computer Interaction (HCI)","Human-Machine Interaction","Purification Work","Science and Technology Studies (STS)","Siri"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-81A09760DCEAA96BDB875117C48CF027"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of california","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"intel labs","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Intel Labs","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lucian","key":"leahupau","last":"Leahu","name":"Leahu, Lucian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marisa","key":"cohnpau","last":"Cohn","locid":"e9d14210-bc71-4824-b7cf-fd1448d022ab","name":"Cohn, Marisa","orcid":"0000-0002-3912-2166","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Wendy","key":"marchpau","last":"March","name":"March, Wendy","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2470654.2466455","isbn":["9781450318990"],"pages":"3331-3334","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the SIGCHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-36c4b47b-7301-4a90-9d8f-df47395749fa"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"How categories come to matter","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382075","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
